-- avg/ is fold-and-finish (sum-fold over count-fold, one finishing divide); #/ is the sum-fold of the mask (spec §12, pre-renumbering §11). Twin of 032-avg-fold-finish.bqn. (was s11-avg-fold-finish)
-- A herd of cows on a scale, their mean weight asked three ways. avg/ is not a primitive fold — the mean of means is not the mean — so it decomposes into the two honest folds and one finishing divide.
-- The third query pins the sum-fold half separately (the .bqn's 2400); the count-fold half is #/ Cow itself.
-- Omitted, left to the .bqn twin: the pairwise-mean associativity-failure witness (675 vs 550; raw associations 512.5 / 712.5), the raw-fold empty identities, and the avg empty-scope row failure — internal counterexamples of the wrong form, and a failed row has no --! spelling.
--! registry ../registries/032-avg-fold-finish.reg

--! out 600
avg/ Weight @ Cow

--! out 4
#/ Cow

--! out 2400
+/ Weight @ Cow
